      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Some worlds have button to reduce brightness in the world. It's part of postprocessing.\nSo i think this is more question for world creators... and much quicker too. And some headsets have own feature to control the brightness of displays.\nI am sure there is also tool in Steam who can control the brightness and colors in VR. \"LuxVR\" in Steam has feature to reduce brightness and also day/night colors.\nSo no really need to change in VRChat itself. Sleeping is not the part of VRChat, it's because you choose do it. Most people don't sleep in VRChat.\nUse 3rd party tool like LuxVR or built-in feature of some headset software will already fix the problem for you. LuxVR is even free. There are already reactions they can sleep better with LuxVR. It's only it's not much known tool...\nYou can even add black screen overlay on your avatar.... to simulate darker screen for your view, and others can see you're sleeping. Easy.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
